{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/907577-shapeshifting-how-does-it-work","id":907577,"title":"Shapeshifting, how does it work?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-06-05T05:45:13-07:00","id":907577,"title":"Shapeshifting, how does it work?","content":"The concept of shapeshifting in the Scion universe confuses me, mostly because of some contradicting details regarding it. I actually would like to play a character who becomes known for their shapeshifting talents, but as it currently stands, the book does not offer a proper explanation on how to go about doing so. <br /> <br /> The God book explains that Gods exist in a sort of incoporeal state in their natural forms, and whatever physical shape they have is created by them with the help of Legend. However, some deities are described as being skilled shapeshifters who are capable of taking a wide variety of forms.<br /> <br /> It is not exactly clear on whether this means those Gods are prone to reconstructing themselves, or if this is some kind of Boon / Knack that enables them to do so. As a trickster deity, Loki is perhaps notorious for his art of disguise. Yet he doesn't have either the Animal Purview or the Epic Appearance knacks that would enable him to alter his physical form.<br /> <br /> Which brings me to my current theory in that regular shapeshifting is an ability that all Gods have, but most don't really care about. It's also purely cosmetic, altering only their outward appearance while everything else stays the same. Mechanical shapeshifting (giving you the capabilities of your disguise) is the result of the user subtly applying Boons and Knacks to their new form. <br /> <br /> For example, the God might take the form of a winged dragon. But when they attempt to fly, they would actually be using the Wind's Freedom boon from the Sky purview, while the use of claws and tail would be part of the Animal Aspect boon from the Animal purview. The armored protection of their scales would be the work of the Epic Stamina knacks.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately this theory doesn't hold up, as it means the character would have to have a very wide range of Boons, Epics and Knacks in order to play a convincing shapeshifter. The animal part could be resolved through the Protean Understanding boon, but that is all the way up at level 10, which means I would have to be a top tier character by the time I got my hands on it. And as I understand it, running a campaign can take months / years to reach Godhood, never mind reaching the Legend cap.<br /> <br /> <br /> So if there is anybody out there more experienced in Scion who can tell me how shapeshifting works, or at least your house ruled versions of it, I would appreciate the help!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-05T15:09:34-07:00","id":907913,"title":"","content":"Shapeshifting in Scion 1e is a bit odd. It isn't like you are a Lord of Chaos from Zelazny's Amber novels. <br /> <br /> Let's clear a few things up though. Loki doesn't have the Animal purview associated with him but he has many Animal boons including Animal Aspect and Protean Understanding as per his writeup in God pg 254. He also has the Epic Appearance knacks of Detail Variation, My Eyes Are Up Here, Perfect Actor, Tailor Made and Undeniable Resemblance). So he has more than enough to pull off many disguises. <br /> <br /> Mechanical shapeshifting basically works for the Animal Purview or the Magic Spell Beast Shape found in Ragnarok. The Appearance boons also have this (limited to humanoid shapes but if you turn into a woman you are capable of becoming pregnant and giving birth and becoming a male allows you to father children. <br /> <br /> As to taking the forms of a dragon/demon I guess it depends on the Storyteller and if they are willing to consider legendary creatures as Animals if you are past Legend 9. <br /> <br /> I think what you are talking about may have some play balance issues however. I mean if I were a character that wanted to be a Storm/Protector god, one of my friends wanted to be an Animal/War god and a third wanted to be a Volcano god (Fire/Earth) but then the fourth in the group makes a shapeshifter and can imitate all of their abilities because they take the forms of any animal they want (which immediately surpases the Animal guy who either has to wait until Protean Understanding or buy multiple Animal Boons at the same level to say I'm good with cats and dogs and birds);..or you just start breathing fire because your a dragon...or can fly and hurl lightning because you turn into a Thunderbird....then I would feel like 'Why did I waste all my points when this guy can buy just one ability and pretty much do whatever I can do?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/333-achilles","name":"Achilles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar333_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-05T15:38:24-07:00","id":907932,"title":"","content":"The illusion purview plus Body of Ichor allows for the widest range and cheaper value of shapeshifting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-05T17:09:35-07:00","id":907989,"title":"","content":"Alas, I don't have Scion Ragnarok right now. I want to get my hands on it, though, for those tasty Illusion and Frost purviews, but kind of spent the budget on Hero, Demigod, God and Companion.<br /> <br /> <br /> To clarify, I was asking about how a designated shapeshifter is capable of taking on so many different forms when the capacity to do so appears to be an end game level ability. I just threw out the dragon as an example. I'm not saying I would play a character who can shift between dragon, phoenix, ogre, centaur, and kraken. It's the mechanics behind doing so that I was confused about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-05T17:54:37-07:00","id":908008,"title":"","content":"There are no clear cut mechanics really. Loki, Iktomi, Hermes, Raven, Manannan and Coyote didn't have to go through a 'gaining experience' phase. The stories about them were pretty much you start as a god and these are your abilities now watch me strut my stuff and steal my brother's cattle at one day old or what have you. As a player I think the cheapest way to be a shape shifter type is to buy Beast Shape (Lvl 6) magic spell which you can find <a href=\"http://scion-mmp.wikidot.com/magic-purview\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>. It will let you shift to any animal for a day and between Detail Variation, Perfect Actor, Tailor Made, Undeniable Resemblance and Unusual Alteration you can pretty much be any humanoid race or even copy a person exactly.<br /> <br /> Neall said that Greeks are the 'best' shapeshifters in 2e so I'm guessing that there will be some more rules there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/333-achilles","name":"Achilles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar333_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-06T10:01:01-07:00","id":908409,"title":"","content":"You could say simply that Avatar shapes do not have to be human. In that case, Gods can manifest as a lower-Legend Avatar to become eagles, golden rains, cloaked travelers, or whatever else. Avatar provides a built-in level of shapeshifting, but to change shape the Avatar must be shed and a new one created. Of course, while in an inhuman Avatar, the God is still <i>mechanically</i> the same as they otherwise would be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}